    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d269">

                <pb facs="0473" n="359" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg359"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.7353b/82: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Portuguese Minister</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Alte</hi>)<anchor n="79b" xml:id="d269-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-06-23"><hi rendition="#italic">June 23,
                        1922</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Department informed British Minister at Lisbon is opposing applications of
                    Western Union Telegraph Company and Commercial <pb facs="0474" n="360"
                        xml:id="pg360"/> Cable Company for concessions to land and operate cables at
                    Azores.</p>
                <p>This Government is deeply interested in having favorable and prompt action taken
                    on applications of American companies and would appreciate any action you can
                    take to that end.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d269-f1" n="79b" type="source" xml:id="d269-f1-content">
